00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.495
If you guys have studied Sets, you must've read Set Theory

00:00:03.495 --> 00:00:07.099
which says "Set is a collection of well-defined objects."

00:00:07.099 --> 00:00:09.889
Now, everything in python is an object, and if you all

00:00:09.889 --> 00:00:14.211
want a data entry in python with no repeated entries

00:00:14.211 --> 00:00:17.587
you can make a set, let me give you a good example

00:00:17.587 --> 00:00:23.428
Imagine you need to collect a list of people whose names start with an 'S'

00:00:23.428 --> 00:00:25.679
and you go to different people and ask their names,

00:00:25.679 --> 00:00:29.713
some say 'Shruti', some 'Samarth', and some 'Shubham'

00:00:29.713 --> 00:00:32.479
maybe one of your friends repeats the name 'Shubham'

00:00:32.479 --> 00:00:35.197
and you may not want to add this to the list because

00:00:35.197 --> 00:00:38.357
if 100 people say 'Shubham', there'll be 100 Shubham in the list.

00:00:38.357 --> 00:00:43.743
And if you want the list that you're making to have no repetitions,

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:44.989
We can make 'SETS' for this.

00:00:44.989 --> 00:00:48.485
Let's see the methods of sets and why it's used.

00:00:48.485 --> 00:00:49.671
So hop onto the computer screen and

00:00:49.671 --> 00:00:50.726
LET'S GET STARTED!!

00:01:00.144 --> 00:01:02.060
Many of you may have learned in maths that

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:04.933
Set is a collection of well-defined objects.

00:01:04.933 --> 00:01:07.340
Well, sets in python are the same too.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.931
Now what's the meaning of set, why is it in python

00:01:10.931 --> 00:01:16.329
Sometimes we collect certain values which we don't want to get repeated.

00:01:16.329 --> 00:01:20.626
Imagine I ask you, the employee IDs of those

00:01:20.626 --> 00:01:23.105
who have already received a gift

00:01:23.308 --> 00:01:28.000
Now you're asked to report who has received a gift

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Imagine there's a company that wants to give a thanksgiving gift once,

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.794
and you need to insure that no one receives a gift more than once.

00:01:35.794 --> 00:01:40.498
So every employee with gifts is asked to submit their IDs.

00:01:40.498 --> 00:01:44.077
Now, if we solve this problem through a list, it will be very big

00:01:44.077 --> 00:01:45.550
and it will have repeated values

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:48.698
One employee may take the name of 5 other employees,

00:01:48.698 --> 00:01:51.169
and the other employee repeats the same exact 5 names.

00:01:51.169 --> 00:01:54.060
Or takes 3 out of the 5 names

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.742
This will increase the size of the list

00:01:56.742 --> 00:01:58.969
and more memory will be used, which we don't want

00:01:58.969 --> 00:02:01.651
That's why there's Set data type inside python.

00:02:02.084 --> 00:02:03.902
So how do we make Set?

00:02:03.902 --> 00:02:11.262
So, If I write s={2,4,2,6} and print it.

00:02:11.645 --> 00:02:15.097
In 's' you'll see 2 is being repeated twice but

00:02:15.491 --> 00:02:17.236
the set will take it only once.

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:22.120
So, {2,4,2,6} will be {2,4,6} as you can see., okay.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:25.029
This shows Set doesn't take repeated values.

00:02:25.029 --> 00:02:28.058
So this is a Set of well-defined objects as we know

00:02:28.058 --> 00:02:30.298
Set is a collection of well-defined objects, right.

00:02:30.298 --> 00:02:33.674
And if I talk about Set here

00:02:33.871 --> 00:02:36.852
There are many methods to it, you can add values

00:02:37.354 --> 00:02:41.066
You can do everything that you can do with a list, in a very similar fashion

00:02:41.066 --> 00:02:44.382
except for the fact that there's no value repetition, okay.

00:02:44.382 --> 00:02:47.208
So, sets are unordered collections of data items.

00:02:47.208 --> 00:02:49.627
Here the word 'unordered' is very important, because

00:02:49.627 --> 00:02:51.196
it does not maintain order.

00:02:51.196 --> 00:02:55.613
You can't hope that if 2 comes first then 4, 6 would come next.

00:02:55.613 --> 00:02:58.534
There's no guarantee of maintaining this order.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:00.259
This is something you all need to remember.

00:03:00.259 --> 00:03:04.066
Set items are separated by commas and enclosed within curly brackets {}.

00:03:04.066 --> 00:03:07.370
As I have done here, values are separated by commas and

00:03:07.388 --> 00:03:11.781
instead of the square brackets that we use in our lists,

00:03:11.781 --> 00:03:14.942
or parentheses (), that we use in Tuple,

00:03:14.942 --> 00:03:17.827
here we use curly brackets, kind of like this.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.324
Through this python interpreter understands that we're talking about sets.

00:03:21.755 --> 00:03:25.154
Sets are unchangeable meaning you can't change items of a set

00:03:25.154 --> 00:03:26.113
once they are created.

00:03:26.113 --> 00:03:29.405
And sets don't contain duplicate items.

00:03:29.405 --> 00:03:30.792
Now let's understand this,

00:03:30.792 --> 00:03:32.924
'Sets are unchangeable' which means

00:03:32.924 --> 00:03:36.623
that I can't put 8 in place of 2.

00:03:37.174 --> 00:03:41.591
Once 2 go in the set; consider this a very big bag

00:03:41.591 --> 00:03:46.151
which has many pearls in it, if you put one more, it gets mixed.

00:03:46.151 --> 00:03:49.779
you can't find it and replace it anymore.

00:03:49.779 --> 00:03:51.145
Understand it kind of like that.

00:03:51.145 --> 00:03:59.152
Just as lists have different kinds of data entries, Sets can have them too

00:03:59.152 --> 00:04:02.396
Now see, 'Carla', 19, false, 5,9, 19

00:04:02.396 --> 00:04:04.300
since 19 is repeated it'll come once.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.209
Now 19 can come at the start or at the end.

00:04:07.209 --> 00:04:10.000
Python doesn't guarantee maintained order.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.543
This you should know. Now as you can see, this is the output.

00:04:13.543 --> 00:04:16.703
But in my case, this is the output. Hence no guarantee for order.

00:04:16.703 --> 00:04:21.108
Now, as you can see, when I ran the code, this was the output.

00:04:21.279 --> 00:04:25.014
But now, this is the output, okay.

00:04:25.014 --> 00:04:29.527
Hence no guarantee for order, anything can be put anywhere.

00:04:29.562 --> 00:04:33.584
You can't say that you'll get a maintained order.

00:04:33.584 --> 00:04:35.201
There's no guarantee, okay.

00:04:35.871 --> 00:04:39.069
Here we see that items of the set occur in random order.

00:04:39.069 --> 00:04:41.524
And hence, they can't be accessed using index numbers.

00:04:41.524 --> 00:04:44.457
You can't do that, info 0, info 1, or info 2. No.

00:04:45.307 --> 00:04:47.785
They don't maintain order, okay.

00:04:48.239 --> 00:04:52.955
Also, sets don't allow duplicate values, which we already saw.

